STLC – Software Testing Life Cycle
STLC stands for Software Testing Life Cycle.
It is a step-by-step process or procedure to test a software application.
It contains different stages or phases, such as:
System Study
Prepare Test Plan or Write Test Plan
Write Test Cases
Prepare RTM
Execute Test Cases
Defect Tracking
Test Execution Report
Retrospective Meeting or Postmortem Meeting
These are the stages of STLC.
1. System Study
In this stage, we go through the requirements given by the customer and understand how the system works.
Test engineers will study and understand the requirements before starting the testing process.
This whole process is called System Study.
2. Prepare Test Plan or Write Test Plan
A Test Plan is a document prepared by the Senior Test Engineer, Senior Test Manager, Test Lead, or experienced people.
It explains the overall testing approach and planning for the project.
This document is called the Test Plan.
3. Write Test Cases
A test case is a step-by-step process or procedure used to test an application.
In this stage, once we go through the requirements, we identify the test scenarios and convert them into test cases.
To write test cases, we need:
Requirements
Test Case Template
Test Scenarios
Tools used:
Jira
QC
ALM
These tools are used to write and manage test cases.
4. Prepare RTM
RTM stands for Requirement Traceability Matrix.
It is a document prepared to check whether each and every requirement has at least one test case or not.
To prepare RTM, we need:
Requirements
Test Cases
This document helps us ensure that all requirements are covered by test cases.
5. Execute Test Cases
Once the requirements are given to the Test Engineers, they write test cases for the application.
After developers develop the application, Test Engineers execute the test cases.
The actual results are compared with the expected results.
If Expected Result and Actual Result are the same, the status will be PASS.
If Expected Result and Actual Result are not the same, the status will be FAIL.
This process is called Execute Test Cases.
To execute test cases, we need:
Test Cases
Software Application
This is where exactly the software is tested.
This is the most important phase of STLC because we find the maximum number of bugs during this phase.
6. Defect Tracking
While executing test cases, if we find any defects, those defects will be reported to the developers.
Now, the Test Engineer should track what is happening with the defect.
They will check whether the developer has fixed the defect or not.
This process is called Defect Tracking.
7. Test Execution Report
This report tells us about the total number of test cases executed.
It also tells us:
Total number of test cases executed.
How many test cases are passed.
How many test cases are failed.
This report will be prepared during the project and also at the end of the project.
It can be prepared by:
Test Engineer
Test Manager
Test Lead
Senior Experienced People
Until this stage, the customer can be involved and can ask for all the documents.
This stage is the last stage for the customer.
8. Retrospective Meeting or Postmortem Meeting
Once everything is completed, all the team members will gather together.
Team members include:
Test Engineer
Developer
Manager
Business Analyst
They will discuss the good things that happened in the project and the improvements needed in the project.
These points will be considered for future projects.
This whole process is called Retrospective Meeting or Postmortem Meeting.
The entire process is called Software Testing Life Cycle (STLC).
